WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.983
- No.

00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:03.081
(laughing)

00:00:03.081 --> 00:00:04.660
I wasn't recording this whole time.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.370
Oh, that's so stupid.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.630
I imagine you're this guy

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.970
and you've been putting off writing

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.950
a thank you letter to your grandma.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.920
She sent you socks or
something for Christmas.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.690
You even went and bought
the stationery to do it.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.340
You have the thank you letter,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.390
nicely wrapped in, but what anyway.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.660
So basically every time
you think about doing it,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.520
you start to feel this
inner sense of resistance.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.140
It's a resistance you
can't seem to break past.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.440
So instead of dealing
with that resistance,

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.440
you go and do an escapist activity

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.010
like playing Apex Legends.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.200
So let's continue this
role play a little bit.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.680
You're playing Apex Legends
for a couple of hours

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.950
and things are going well
and then it hits you.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.210
It's an inner kind of
disgusting, guilty feeling.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.240
It says if the anxiety of the thing

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.210
that you're avoiding starts
to pervade the activity

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.320
that you're using to escape
the thing you're avoiding.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.230
Congratulations, in this
short little role-playing,

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.470
totally fictional experiment we just did.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.050
You just experienced
the two types of pain,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.270
the pain of action and
the pain of inaction.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.630
The pain of action is something
we can all identify with.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.130
It's that discomfort we feel

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.170
before we do anything constructive.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.960
Anytime you think about doing
something that's constructive

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.670
and a little bit difficult,
there's that inner sense

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.970
of resistance that seems
to stop you from doing it.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.880
And in order to actually
accomplish that thing,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.590
you have to break through that resistance

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:23.500
and then you get it done.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.500
That inner sense of resistance is like

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.330
it's a paralyzing feeling.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.440
Breaking through this resistance usually

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.670
takes some good old
white knuckle willpower.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.250
So while it's painful and
uncomfortable up front,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.850
if you just take it on
the chin and deal with it,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.280
you start to become stronger
and more able to deal

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.420
with it in the future.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.140
You start to become somebody
who is okay with discomfort,

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.220
your confidence, your self efficacy,

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.950
and basically your whole life improves

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.670
because not only do you
feel better about yourself,

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.420
usually doing something constructive

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.920
makes your life situation better anyways.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.760
It's kind of like a lose, win.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.110
The lose is eating the pain
and the win is the redemption

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.570
that comes from that pain.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.950
So that's the pain of action.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.720
The pain of inaction is far more subtle

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.710
and it's a lot more sinister too.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.080
And that's because it doesn't
usually feel like pain at all.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.680
When you choose to play Apex,
instead of filing your taxes,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.077
it may actually feel good for a while.

00:02:18.077 --> 00:02:19.960
And it's a lot more fun to play Apex

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.160
than it is to file your taxes,

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.760
but kind of like binge
drinking on a Friday night,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.120
you're just stealing the
happiness from Saturday morning.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.260
And the debt you'll
have to repay afterwards

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.100
is far more painful than
just taking the initial pain

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.330
on the chin to begin with.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:39.330
The pain of inaction is a slow
burning, degenerative pain

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.730
that ruins every aspect of your life.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:45.950
By choosing the inaction route,
you become a softer person,

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.630
somebody who flinches at
the site of discomfort,

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.920
somebody who can't get stuff done.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.840
And the consequence of that
on a long enough timeline

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.760
is you start to dislike yourself,

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.620
you start to not believe in
your ability to get things done

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.360
and your life starts to
fall apart around you.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.500
You'll eventually dig
yourself into a hole so deep

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.540
that it seems impossible to get out of

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.110
until you're pained by the
misery of your own existence.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.290
Obviously this is really morbid,
but it's nonetheless true.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.060
Nobody can avoid pain in day-to-day life.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.120
Pain is just something that
we all have to deal with,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.940
but thankfully we can choose
which pain we deal with.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.760
If you choose not to fool yourself

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.590
and take the pain right up front,

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.450
battle through the discomfort
of taking constructive action,

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.530
then you won't have this
massive pain debt to pay.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.880
And the pain debt is the pain of inaction,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.140
which is a lot more crappy in general.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.558
So yeah, that's all I got
to say is choose wisely.

00:03:38.558 --> 00:03:39.391
(chuckles)

00:03:39.391 --> 00:03:40.970
I think that's pretty
much all I'm gonna say.

